Here's the complete `pilot/index.ts` implementing that salvage loop:

```ts
import {
  goTo,
  salvage,
  disengage,
  sell,
  orient,
  note,
  isError,
} from 'play';

export default async function main() {
  // Salvage everything we can get. Re-arrives at the POI via goTo; each
  // iteration the game decides whether the fresh actions succeed. Loops are
  // capped so a persistent failure surfaces rather than spinning forever.
  const MAX_SALVAGE_LOOPS = 20;
  const MAX_DISENGAGE_LOOPS = 10;
  let salvages = 0;

  for (let loop = 0; loop < MAX_SALVAGE_LOOPS; loop++) {
    // Make sure we are actually at the debris field (docked there first turn,
    // so this no-ops; otherwise it flies us back after a base round-trip).
    await goTo('sol_debris');

    let battleRetries = 0;
    let ok = false;
    while (!ok) {
      try {
        await salvage();
        salvages++;
        ok = true;
      } catch (e) {
        if (isError(e, 'NoWreck')) {
          note('no wreck');
          return;
        }
        if (isError(e, 'InBattle')) {
          if (battleRetries++ >= MAX_DISENGAGE_LOOPS) throw e; // give up if we can never clear combat
          await disengage();
          continue; // salvage again
        }
        if (isError(e, 'HoldFull')) {
          // No room: take everything to base, sell it, come back, salvage again.
          await goTo('sol_base');
          const hold = (await orient()).cargo;
          if (hold.length > 0) {
            await sell(hold); // omit quantity => all of it
          }
          await goTo('sol_debris');
          ok = true; // run the loop again to salvage with the now-open hold
          continue;
        }
        // Any other typed error (NotAtBelt, ServerBusy, BadData...): nothing in
        // the spec to handle here, so let it propagate as the failure.
        throw e;
      }
    }
  }

  throw new Error(`could not salvage within ${MAX_SALVAGE_LOOPS} loops`);
}
```

A couple of notes on the design:

- **`NoWreck`** — we `note('no wreck')` and `return` immediately, so the run finishes without failing.
- **`InBattle`** — we `disengage()` then loop straight back into `salvage()`, which is exactly the "disengage and salvage again" ask. A cap (`MAX_DISENGAGE_LOOPS`) is there only as a safety valve; a normal fight clears in one retry.
- **`HoldFull`** — we `goTo('sol_base')`, `sell(hold)` (omitting `quantity` so it's "everything in the hold"), `goTo('sol_debris')`, and loop to salvage again. The `if (hold.length > 0)` guard avoids a pointless `sell` that would reject with `NoBuyer` if the hold happened to be empty.

I called `sell(hold)` with the rows read from `orient()` rather than a hand-rolled item list, because "sell everything in the hold" is exactly what that does.

