It fires all three calls at once with `Promise.all` (before any `await` on their results, so they truly start together), then notes the requested line. I also added a tiny defensive guard: if `prices()` is legitimately empty, the reducer picks the first item (none) and we note `0` credits, `—` as the top item, and the real mission count, rather than crashing on `.item_id`.

```ts
import {orient, prices, missions, note} from 'play';

export default async function main() {
  // Kick off all three concurrent calls at once.
  // The Promise.all is created synchronously before any result is awaited,
  // so the runtime starts the orient/prices/missions actions together.
  const [pres, quotes, tasks] = await Promise.all([orient(), prices(), missions()]);

  // Item with the highest best_buy (0 if there is nothing at all).
  const top = quotes.reduce<{item_id: string; best_buy: number}>((acc, q) =>
    q.best_buy > acc.best_buy ? {item_id: q.item_id, best_buy: q.best_buy} : acc,
    {item_id: '', best_buy: -Infinity}
  );
  const topLabel = top.item_id === '' ? '—' : top.item_id;

  note(`credits ${pres.credits} · top best_buy ${topLabel} · ${tasks.length} missions`);
}
```

